<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Horacio Vásquez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1860">1860</a>–<a href="/years/1936">1936</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Horacio Vásquez was a Dominican general and politician who served briefly as provisional president in 1899 and 1902–1903. Elected president in 1924, his victory ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> military occupation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a>. His attempt to extend his term weakened his government, and in 1930 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafael-trujillo">Rafael Trujillo</a> forced him out.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/horacio-vasquez.jpg" alt="Horacio Vásquez" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Horacio_V%C3%A1zquez_1924.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
